menu "ReAir"
    config REAIR_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "Button GPIO"
        range 0 48
        default 0
        help
            GPIO of the on-board button, active low with internal pull-up.
            Set per target in sdkconfig.defaults.<target>: this pin is also a
            strapping pin, so the board's BOOT button is used on dev boards.

    config REAIR_FAN_PWM_GPIO
        int "Fan PWM GPIO (-1: no fan)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            GPIO driving the N-channel MOSFET that pulls the fan PWM line low
            (ADR 0005). The output is inverted in firmware to compensate.

    config REAIR_LED_GPIO
        int "Status LED GPIO (-1: no LED)"
        range -1 48
        default -1
        help
            Active-low status LED (ADR 0006): anode to 3.3V through a resistor,
            cathode to this pin. On ESP32-C3 this is GPIO8, a strapping pin that
            must stay high at reset.

    config REAIR_OTA_SELFTEST_TIMEOUT_S
        int "OTA self test timeout (seconds)"
        range 10 600
        default 60
        help
            After an OTA update the new firmware must pass the hardware self
            test (ADR 0007) within this time, otherwise the bootloader rolls
            back to the previous firmware.
endmenu
